id: pm-github-xcr3
title: Honor caller changelog policy in gated sync and closeout
description: "Use the caller's changelog scripts for gated sync and closeout, and validate regenerated output before publication."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: changelog-unreleased,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#226"
created_at: "2026-11-18T09:38:46.683Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T20:14:12.268Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[9]:
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T09:39:06.130Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Both reusable workflows regenerate after the tracker writes, but inject a pending-release override for changelog:full. Run the declared caller script and its optional changelog:check before the existing privacy scan, then keep the regenerated changelog in the tracker commit. Preserve the no-tracker-change publication path."
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T09:42:09.908Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: Confirmed tracker_changed in the audit-windows log for pm-brief#224 and the test (22) log for pm-context#222. The baseline closeout discard branch runs only when the workflow has no closeout proposal. Preserve that behavior and keep both changelogs with the corresponding tracker edits.
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T09:53:26.995Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "The closeout log for pm-context#222 compares committed Unreleased with the caller check's expected 2026.11.16 heading. Both scripts now use npm run --if-present with no generator arguments, then run the caller check before scope and privacy validation. Tagged and untagged placement cases passed. The candidate includes the regenerated Unreleased fix, caller upgrade documentation, and default-versus-wrapper coverage."
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T09:59:01.555Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "The commit Honor caller changelog policy in gated sync and closeout contains both workflow changes, the contract tests, the generated changelog entry, and the upgrade notes. Focused workflow publication and refusal tests passed 4/4. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, identity inventory, changelog:check, and the isolated candidate privacy scan passed. The full affected-file command is linked and running through pm test. The final commit is checked in an isolated clone before the branch push."
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T10:09:16.341Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "The production caller check can print a generated changelog diff. Move the check after the first full changed-path/privacy scan so the check sees scanned output, and keep the existing final pre-commit scan. This refinement keeps the publication veto before token minting and commit."
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T10:11:30.586Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: The follow-up uses a dedicated Check caller changelog policy step after initial privacy validation. The sync privacy fixture asserts that a refused changelog cannot reach the caller check. Restarted the linked affected-file run at the CI quick depth on the revised code.
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T10:19:45.122Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "The follow-up commit Scan tracker changes before the caller changelog check keeps both scans in place. The revised workflow and caller-policy contract tests passed 11/11, including privacy refusal before the check, no remote write on caller policy failure, and combined tracker and changelog commits. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, workflow Bash syntax, identity inventory, and changelog:check passed. The linked 26-file CI-depth run is in progress."
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T12:50:13.786Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Round CD maps all four threads to the commit Skip caller changelog checks on no-op tracker runs. PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM646cFC guards sync and closeout policy checks with the staged tracker publication criteria. Both no-op regressions reproduced the failure on 7e09e9e and now verify that the stale review closes while publication is skipped. The closeout mutation test targets the publication guard explicitly and passes. PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM646cFS restores the one-release and no-delivery-in-release assertions. PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM646UJH aligns wrapper guidance with the caller check. PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM646cFI limits wrapper removal to pure delegation and documents how to retain wrapper flags and environment. All 10 focused tests and the targeted mutation retest passed. Typecheck, test build, lint, docstrings, privacy, identity inventory and changelog regeneration and check passed. The linked 26-file full-depth run is active."
    edited_at: "2026-11-18T13:00:12.485Z"
  - created_at: "2026-11-18T20:14:04.214Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Round CJ maps PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM64_pr5, PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM64_psG, and PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM65CYhO to the commit Bind workflow publication to the caller changelog check. The sync and closeout workflows preserve npm lifecycle hooks, compare the scoped index and worktree before and after the check, and verify the receipt before staging and commit. The closeout no-op test compares changelog bytes and checks the full index. The README requires the wrapper lifecycle hooks to be absent before removing the override. The generated release section and ownership anchor were refreshed. Typecheck, build, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, inventory, changelog check, and the supplemental 13 tests passed. The focused and full workflow test commands are linked and running directly."
